    fix(sessions): resolve an uncached New Chat and carry the fork open-suppression across the picker handoff
    
    Follow-ups from the gate certification on this head:
    
    - Resolve the handed-off session from S.session when the visible active
      New Chat has no messages and is not in the session cache yet. The cache
      and child lookups keep precedence and the connected-anchor validation
      is unchanged, so the action menu opens on the first click again after
      the deferred repaint.
    - Move a pending _skipNextChildOpen from the pressed fork row to the row
      that replaced it during the deferred-repaint handoff, so the release
      click is consumed once and the parent session stays active instead of
      the fork opening.
    - Added checked-in behavioral regressions for both schedules: an uncached
      New Chat handoff (desktop and mobile viewports) and a fork long-press
      release with real touch input (phone and tablet viewports), plus
      Node-harness handoff cases for both.
    
