**One gap in the repaint deferral that #6713 introduced (SILENT): the sidebar can stay stale after the picker is abandoned for another row's menu.** While the "Move to project" picker is open, sidebar repaints are deferred (`static/sessions.js` ~8346) and replayed when the picker closes. Clicking another row's **⋮** button stops click propagation, so the picker's outside-click teardown never runs. That ⋮ menu then closes, but its repaint is skipped because `_projectPickerTeardown` is still set, and the deferred flag stays set. Codex drove it in Chromium on this merged tree with real clicks and Escape: the parent row and a nested child row kept their old labels and the deferred flag remained set. Master has no deferral, so this can't happen there.

This is the "two popovers open" case Fable listed as a pre-existing follow-up. With the deferral in place it also leaves archive/pin/rename updates unpainted until the picker is closed some other way.

**Fix (small):** at the top of `_openSessionActionMenu` (~5451), retire an active picker synchronously: `if (_projectPickerTeardown) { const t = _projectPickerTeardown; _projectPickerTeardown = null; t(); }`, so its deferred repaint replays. Please add a regression that opens the picker, triggers a deferred repaint, clicks another row's real ⋮, closes that menu, and asserts the parent and nested child repaint and the flag clears.

