fix(sessions): return focus after a deferred repaint, open for stale anchors, scroll clear of the pinned footer

Follow-ups from the browser keyboard gate on the merged tree:

- dismiss() now paints a sidebar repaint that the open picker deferred,
  before restoring focus, so Escape lands on the row's newly rendered
  trigger instead of an element the repaint is about to replace.
- The picker opens even when its anchor was replaced or clipped before
  the call (selection-mode repaints rebuild rows first). The observer
  and the scroll/resize listeners keep owning its lifecycle.
- The scrolling picker sets scroll-padding-bottom, so rows scrolled to
  the bottom edge stay clear of the pinned "+ New project" footer and
  remain tappable.

