<!-- handoff-repairs-2026-10-10:start -->
## Gate follow-up — the two remaining handoff regressions (2026-10-10)

The latest gate certification found two remaining picker-to-menu handoff regressions after the earlier scoped repairs landed. Published `31322828a1c6565af966b885aa99c2ec58c3469e` as a fast-forward on top of `3cfc7612…` (tree `4a418f2b8293ef93a9ba6022062aefb0eccef1ee`); no history rewrite.

- **A New Chat the cache has not seen yet**: an active New Chat with no messages renders from `S.session` but is not in the session cache, so after a deferred repaint its first ⋮ click closed the picker without opening the menu. The handoff now resolves the session from `S.session` when the id matches, after the cache/child lookups and with the connected-anchor validation unchanged.
- **Fork long-press release after the repaint**: the deferred repaint replaced the pressed fork row, and the pending one-click open-suppression stayed on the detached row, so the browser's release click opened the fork. The handoff now moves the pending `_skipNextChildOpen` to the replacement row, where the existing one-click consumption applies.
- **Checked-in regressions for both schedules**: an uncached New Chat handoff (desktop and mobile viewports) and a fork long-press release driven by Chromium touch input (phone and tablet viewports), with the fork row's open handler extracted from production; plus two Node-harness handoff cases.

Verification on this head:

- RED proof before the change: the four new browser cases and both Node cases fail on `3cfc7612`; after the change the focus and picker suites pass (**54 passed**).
- Sweeps: `test_session_*`/`test_sidebar_*` **1045 passed, 8 skipped**; menu/mobile/anchor/touch **560 passed, 1 skipped**; all `*picker*` files plus the project-chip suite **298 passed**.
- `npm run lint:runtime`, `node --check static/sessions.js`, Ruff on the changed tests, and `git diff --check`: clean.

CI re-runs on this head; the maintainer re-gate remains the next step.
<!-- handoff-repairs-2026-10-10:end -->

<!-- keyboard-gate-followup-2026-10-10:start -->
## Keyboard-gate follow-up — the three remaining failures (2026-10-10)

The repository's browser gates caught three interactions that were still failing on this head; this update carries the fixes for all three. Published `3cfc761297043efb30a7fd7aaa3facd835856604` as a fast-forward on top of `08ed3c9e…` (tree `343f6a002dff658ee4982dc05c6ad6335c3b7c2a`); no history rewrite.

- **Escape after a sidebar repaint**: a repaint deferred while the picker was open was replayed *after* focus was restored, so Escape dropped focus to the page instead of the conversation's new ⋮ trigger. The deferred repaint is now painted before focus returns, and focus resolves to the row the sidebar shows afterwards (a parent row resolves to its own trigger, not a fork's).
- **Opening from a row rebuilt mid-flow**: the picker closed itself when its anchor had already been replaced or clipped by an earlier repaint (for example a selection-mode rebuild). It now opens, and its observer and scroll/resize listeners keep owning the lifecycle.
- **Rows under the pinned "+ New project" footer**: in a capped, scrolling picker the pinned footer covered the bottom band, so rows scrolled to the bottom edge could not be tapped. The picker now sets `scroll-padding-bottom`, so scrolled rows land clear of the pinned footer.

Verification on this head, with real Chromium (the same gates the repository runs):

- `python tests/browser_project_picker_keyboard.py`: **PROJECT PICKER KEYBOARD PASSED** — every scenario, including the four phone viewports and the tall-anchor long lists.
- `python tests/browser_smoke.py`: all pages, zero console errors.
- `./scripts/test.sh` (21 picker/menu/session/sidebar files): **378 passed, 1 skipped**; `test_session_*`/`test_sidebar_*`: **1041 passed, 8 skipped**; menu/mobile/anchor/touch suites: **556 passed, 1 skipped**.
- `npm run lint:runtime`, `node --check static/sessions.js`, `git diff --check`: clean.

CI re-runs on this head; the maintainer re-gate remains the next step.
<!-- keyboard-gate-followup-2026-10-10:end -->

<!-- review-followup-2026-10-10:start -->
## Review follow-up — fallback placement, queued close checks, and context-point tracking (2026-10-10)

Published `08ed3c9ed0a4f944825fab454e9abcbb6270d85a` as a history-preserving fast-forward from reviewed head `5f141ce4b5672cc5a3a6dcd764764d52f095a854`; no history rewrite. The uploaded Git tree `a38305186ff502ee2914d01c0ddd4f1d3b87d887` is byte-identical to the locally tested tree.

- Applied the shared width cap and horizontal clamp in the no-`visualViewport` fallback, including narrow-window containment.
- Coalesced queued reposition requests without losing a later scroll-close requirement; the pending state is consumed/reset by the frame and cleared during teardown.
- Stored right-click coordinates relative to the owning parent/fork row and rebuilt current screen coordinates from the row's latest rectangle, so a partially scrolled row keeps the picker attached.
- Added production-function regressions for fallback horizontal placement, narrow containment, both viewport/scroll event orders with cleanup, and partial-scroll context tracking.

Verification:

- RED proof on the prior production code: **5 failed, 37 passed** for the expanded viewport-positioning suite.
- Final related suites: **103 passed, 6 skipped** across viewport positioning, action-menu focus, touch actions, pin caps, and picker keyboard/accessibility coverage. The skips are the existing browser-dependency guard in this environment.
- `node --check static/sessions.js`, `npm run lint:runtime`, Ruff on the changed tests, and `git diff --check`: passed.
- Fresh GitHub CI and maintainer re-review remain pending.
<!-- review-followup-2026-10-10:end -->

## Conflict resolution — merged upstream master (2026-10-10)

The branch was rebuilt on current `master` (`1da79492`) with a normal two-parent merge commit; no history rewrite. Upstream's project-picker keyboard work (#8044 and its follow-ups) had reworked the same area since the last integration (`cc468a41`), so `static/sessions.js` needed a semantic merge.

What the resolution keeps:

- This PR's viewport-aware behavior: visual-viewport bounds (on-screen keyboard, URL bar, pinch zoom), session-list scroll tracking that closes the picker when its row leaves the list, the coarse-pointer context-point anchoring, the skipped-repaint replay, and the centralized teardown.
- Upstream's newer picker architecture: keyboard navigation (#8044), the resize hook that re-places an open picker by its conversation's current row, focus return, the hidden-sidebar dismissal, and the translated labels.
- Placement order: below the anchor, else above it, else slid up from the bottom edge to fit; the height cap and internal scrolling stay for lists taller than the visible screen.

Verification on the merged tree (all green):

- `./scripts/test.sh` over 21 picker/menu/session/sidebar files: **368 passed, 7 skipped** — including this PR's picker suite (38 passed) and upstream's `test_issue8044_project_picker_a11y.py` (30 passed).
- Wider sweeps: **1014 passed** across `test_session_*` and `test_sidebar_*`; **538 passed** across the menu/mobile/anchor/touch suites.
- `npm run lint:runtime`, `node --check static/sessions.js`, and `git diff --check`: clean.
- Real-browser coverage (`tests/browser_project_picker_keyboard.py`) runs in this repository's `browser-smoke` workflow for this head; it was not runnable locally (no Chromium in the merge environment).

## Thinking Path

The latest review identified two remaining gaps: visual-viewport events recomputed layout-viewport geometry, and scrolling the session list did not update its body-mounted picker. Sidebar renders could also leave an orphan until another viewport event.

This follow-up fixes those ownership and geometry gaps in the existing single-session picker.

