Resolved the exact-head gate finding at `9192f32f9c7958303aff73b119f440c20e94c6a3`.

- A hidden project-picker anchor now resolves the nearest connected fork-child row before the ancestor session item, so an expanded viewport-spanning parent can no longer make the fork child's **Move to project** action silently no-op.
- The fork-child mouse context-menu path now records the trusted click point, matching the parent-row path while retaining the child row as the lifecycle/visibility owner.
- Added a compact 390×620 regression with a 1,269px expanded parent and visible fork child. It verifies contained placement and verifies teardown once the child itself scrolls offscreen; a source guard covers the fork context-point handoff.

