### Repaint context-point handoff follow-up (2026-10-02)

Resolved the latest coarse-pointer handoff case at `b7adf70f196842f635b5711c3931e8331f2c30d9`.

- The action-menu handoff now snapshots the trusted right-click point before retiring picker A and transfers it to the newly rendered row B actions anchor.
- The refreshed anchor therefore preserves precise placement instead of falling back to the expanded parent row and immediately failing the visibility guard.
- Regression coverage verifies the new connected anchor receives the original `clientX/clientY` point while the canonical nested session and action-menu ownership are handed off.

Verification: **49 passed, 3 skipped** across project-picker positioning, touch actions, and action-menu focus; `node --check static/sessions.js`, Ruff, and `git diff --check` passed. GitHub CI and maintainer re-gate are pending.


